  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Disproportionation reaction, also sometimes called dismutation reaction, is basically&nbsp;a type of redox reaction involving simultaneous reduction and oxidation of atoms of the same element from one oxidation state (OS) to two different oxidation states.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mn>3</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><msub><mi>MnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>"
